  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The direct cause was a fatigue crack propagated through the stem of AEFCV0520, causing the stem to fracture, resulting in a loss of feed flow control to the 'B' Steam Generator. The root cause was tool marks within the thread root caused local stress risers, which allowed multiple cracks to initiate. In addition, the thread root was also cut deeper and narrower than allowed by specification.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "manufacturing defect (thread tool marks/undersized root) causing fatigue crack and valve stem fracture",
    "provisional": true
